license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization that, for every positive integer n, the minimum
  size of a critical set among Latin squares of order n, and in the cyclic
  Latin square, is floor(n squared / 4), together with the parity theorem
  that fewer than floor(n squared / 4) filled cells give an even number of
  completions. Includes the unrestricted lower bound, a cyclic corner
  construction, a restatement with the paper's own definitions, and checked
  axiom reports. Substantially AI-generated (Codex for version 0.1.0, Claude
  for the version 0.2.0 additions) under Richard Bean's direction; see
  README.md for provenance and the precise scope of the formalization.
keywords:
  - Latin squares
  - critical sets
